-- title:
--   Mod-𝔪 eigenvalue system yields a maximal ideal of the Hecke algebra
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, $N'\ge 1$, $k\in\mathbb Z$, and let $S_0\subseteq\mathbb N$ contain every prime divisor of $N'$. Let $c\in\mathbb N$ be such that no prime $\ell\notin S_0$ with $\ell\nmid N'$ divides $c$, and let $\mathfrak m$ be a maximal ideal of the integral closure $\bar{\mathbb Z}$ of $\mathbb Z$ in $\mathbb C$ with $p\in\mathfrak m$. Let $G$ be a cusp form of weight $k$ for $\Gamma_0(N')$ whose $q$-expansion coefficients $a_n(G)=$ `qCoeff G n` satisfy: for every $n$ coprime to $c$ there are $x,y\in\bar{\mathbb Z}$ with $y\notin\mathfrak m$ and $x=y\,a_n(G)$, and for at least one such $n$ these can be chosen with $x\notin\mathfrak m$ as well. Let $a:\mathbb N\to\mathbb Z$ and let $Q$ be a predicate on $\mathbb N$, and assume that for every prime $\ell\notin S_0$ with $\ell\nmid N'$ there is $e\in\bar{\mathbb Z}$ such that $Q(\ell)$ implies $e-a(\ell)\in\mathfrak m$, and such that for all $n$ coprime to $c$ and all $x,x',y\in\bar{\mathbb Z}$ with $y\notin\mathfrak m$, $x=y\,a_n(\mathrm{T}_\ell G)$ and $x'=y\,a_n(G)$ one has $x-e\,x'\in\mathfrak m$; here $\mathrm{T}_\ell$ is the element `heckeAlgebra.T hℓ hℓN hℓS` of the Hecke algebra `heckeAlgebra N' k S₀` acting through its coercion to $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb C}S_k(\Gamma_0(N'))$, and `heckeAlgebra N' k S₀` is the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb C}S_k(\Gamma_0(N'))$ generated by the operators `heckeTLin k hℓ hℓN` for primes $\ell\nmid N'$, $\ell\notin S_0$ together with the operators `heckeULin k hqN` for primes $q\mid N'$, $q\notin S_0$ (the latter set being empty under the hypothesis on $S_0$). Then there is a maximal ideal $\mathfrak m_k$ of `heckeAlgebra N' k S₀` containing the image of $p$ and containing $\mathrm{T}_\ell-a(\ell)$ for every prime $\ell\notin S_0$ with $\ell\nmid N'$ such that $Q(\ell)$ holds.
--
--   This is the passage from a system of mod-$\mathfrak m$ Hecke eigenvalues, recorded on the $q$-expansion coefficients at indices prime to $c$, to a residual maximal ideal of the anemic Hecke algebra of level $N'$ and weight $k$ with prescribed traces $a(\ell)$ at the primes where $Q$ holds. It is used in the level-lowering part of the argument, by [`WeierstrassCurve.exists_ideal_heckeAlgebra_ordCompl_of_isNewform_sq_dvd`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.exists_ideal_heckeAlgebra_ordCompl_of_isNewform_sq_dvd).
